module

public import Mathlib
public import LoopEquality.Split16

@[expose] public section

/-!
# l = 16: the shape lists and the kernel checks, in small pieces

With bilayer `0` of letter `0`, the root side is read in `sigR a` (letter `a` at bilayer `-1`) and the far side in
`sigF b` (letter `b` at bilayer `1`). `zqOf b` lists one representative of each class of crossing sets carrying a
meeting pair of far arcs, or the half-turn of one (from `l16/shapes16.py`). The kernel checks, each a small theorem:
every candidate's class is listed (`hcheckF`, one piece per start point of the second arc), the list consists of
normalised, distinct four-point sets (`zq_props`), the far asymmetries (`af_*`) and root weights (`wr_*`) of every
shape and matching, and from these the zero sums (`sum16B_kernel`). Generated by `l16/gen_data16.py`.

With Claude (Anthropic).
-/

